The physical geography of New England is[ diverse] for such a small area.[ S][outheastern] New England is covered by a narrow coastal plain, while the[ western] and northern regions are dominated by the rolling hills and worn-down peaks of the[ northern] end[ of] the Appalachian Mountains[.]
